WEBVTT

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:06.980
Loving another person is
a very good thing, Birdy.

00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:10.050
I love you lots, Violin.

00:00:10.050 --> 00:00:14.190
Thank you. But I think that
love may be a little different...

00:00:14.190 --> 00:00:15.460
Huh?

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:20.450
That feeling is special, and quite wonderful...

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:56.490
I'm going to make you talk about
the Central Tower terrorism, too,

00:01:56.490 --> 00:01:57.830
Valic Nigua.

00:01:57.830 --> 00:01:59.000
Huh?

00:01:59.000 --> 00:02:01.300
Jeez, that again?

00:02:01.300 --> 00:02:06.000
You're sure obsessed with that old story.

00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:11.770
The guy after me was involved
in that incident too, you know.

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:16.280
More importantly, hurry up and
arrest that homicidal lxioran!

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:19.280
He told me he'd kill me last.

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:22.120
Then who's he targeting now?

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:23.920
Gatol and Moss.

00:02:23.920 --> 00:02:26.290
Show me where they are.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:27.260
Birdy!

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:30.460
Ah, I see, that's an idea.

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:34.260
Being with an investigator
would be the safest thing, after all.

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:38.460
Catch Nataru, okay Investigator?
I'm counting on you.

00:02:47.480 --> 00:02:50.610
I'll make you lot understand the
resentment of those who died here,

00:02:50.610 --> 00:02:55.790
and the grief of those left behind...

00:02:55.790 --> 00:02:59.820
By making you fear death!

00:02:59.820 --> 00:03:02.020
I'll kill you.

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.630
That's fine with me.

00:03:03.630 --> 00:03:08.620
Now come on... and try to kill me.

00:03:22.650 --> 00:03:25.480
This had better not be over already.

00:03:30.190 --> 00:03:32.020
Oh, good.

00:03:37.260 --> 00:03:40.400
You have to give me some fun.

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.230
I'll kill you.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:48.700
Not bad! Come on, show me more!

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:57.910
I thought so. In exchange for
the jump abilities you gained,

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:00.680
your biodefense shield is weak.

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:04.520
Now, show me more power. If you don't...

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:10.290
...I can't have any fun!

00:04:10.290 --> 00:04:13.730
I want to see a strong man!

00:04:18.770 --> 00:04:21.760
What's the matter? Is that all you've got?!

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:49.630
This is good. Give me more...

00:04:49.630 --> 00:04:52.740
More...

00:04:52.740 --> 00:04:54.330
I'll kill you.

00:05:42.020 --> 00:05:44.350
I won't kill you easily.

00:05:44.350 --> 00:05:47.790
Ulgarians have a stronger
life force than Altans, after all.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:55.350
I'll make you suffer...

00:05:57.200 --> 00:05:58.390
Nataru!

00:06:02.070 --> 00:06:03.410
Birdy.

00:06:03.410 --> 00:06:07.080
Nataru, let's end this, okay?

00:06:07.080 --> 00:06:10.070
Birdy, you don't understand anything.

00:06:18.350 --> 00:06:21.990
Please, Birdy. Don't interfere.

00:06:21.990 --> 00:06:26.500
The law will punish the criminals!
Leave this to me, Nataru!

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.090
The law? The Federation government's law?

00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:37.210
As in, those guys who oppressed
the Altans and made lxiorans like us?

00:06:37.210 --> 00:06:39.200
Like hell I could believe in them!

00:06:46.780 --> 00:06:48.620
Do you suppose you've saved me?

00:06:48.620 --> 00:06:50.750
I didn't do it to save you.

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:54.020
I just don't want to let Nataru be
responsible for any more crimes.

00:06:54.020 --> 00:06:56.620
No one can stop him now.

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:06.540
Birdy, hand her over.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:09.470
I'll arrest her, so...

00:07:09.470 --> 00:07:11.300
You don't understand anything.

00:07:14.280 --> 00:07:19.250
The Federation could never judge
them for what they did on this planet.

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:21.380
So I'll do it.

00:07:21.380 --> 00:07:25.290
What will that change?
Will it make the dead happy?

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:30.160
Birdy, will you end your life
as a tool of the Federation?

00:07:30.160 --> 00:07:35.160
Working for those guys who treat
the people of Earth like worms?

00:07:35.160 --> 00:07:37.270
Not everyone in the government is like that!

00:07:37.270 --> 00:07:42.300
As an lxioran, you were raised by
the Federation from a young age.

00:07:42.300 --> 00:07:48.780
Think back. You tried to believe
that Violin was a real person.

00:07:48.780 --> 00:07:52.980
Even the feelings of lxiorans
are controlled by others.

00:07:54.780 --> 00:07:59.410
You poor thing... all because you were born lxioran.

00:08:00.760 --> 00:08:03.350
I love you, Birdy.

00:08:04.790 --> 00:08:08.790
I don't want to see you like this anymore.

00:08:15.810 --> 00:08:17.870
So...

00:08:17.870 --> 00:08:19.860
...I'll kill you.

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.290
I thought so.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:32.050
Nataru!

00:08:32.050 --> 00:08:35.890
You're lxioran. So...

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:40.290
Stop it, Nataru!

00:08:42.500 --> 00:08:43.690
Why?!

00:08:51.970 --> 00:08:56.010
Nataru, stop it! Why do we have to fight?!

00:08:56.010 --> 00:09:00.640
Because you're an lxioran.

00:09:09.860 --> 00:09:11.490
Nataru!

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:17.430
That's what being an lxioran is, Birdy.

00:09:17.430 --> 00:09:20.170
On an instinctual level, you want to fight.

00:09:20.170 --> 00:09:27.680
lxiorans are made that way.
They're only kept alive so they can fight.

00:09:27.680 --> 00:09:31.550
I killed them for revenge.

00:09:31.550 --> 00:09:35.920
But somewhere along the line, I started enjoying it.

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:39.760
Enjoying using my lxioran powers.

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:42.560
You like it too, don't you Birdy?

00:09:42.560 --> 00:09:48.060
You enjoy using your lxioran
powers to catch criminals, right?

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:51.570
You end up wanting to fight, right?

00:09:51.570 --> 00:09:55.140
I don't want to see you like that.

00:09:55.140 --> 00:09:56.130
I...

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:32.170
Birdy, why do you run away?

00:10:32.170 --> 00:10:34.080
Birdy, you can't fight him!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:35.910
I know! But...

00:11:00.600 --> 00:11:03.310
Hey, Hayamiya, we really have to get started...

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.440
There are lots of people here.

00:11:05.440 --> 00:11:07.840
The audience is getting impatient, too.

00:11:07.840 --> 00:11:09.610
I won't forgive you for this, Senkawa!

00:11:09.610 --> 00:11:11.600
How dare you stand me up?!

00:11:13.650 --> 00:11:18.850
Two months ago, we experienced
an unprecedented tragedy.

00:11:20.660 --> 00:11:27.060
We lost many people, and
many more were hurt or grieving.

00:11:27.060 --> 00:11:31.630
And yet, that grief was forgotten shockingly fast,

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:36.210
and through the media and the internet,
it was replaced with hatred.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:39.380
We thought that was wrong somehow,

00:11:39.380 --> 00:11:43.310
and we wanted to reexamine
what the tragedy brought us,

00:11:43.310 --> 00:11:47.750
so we interviewed the people
living in the refugee camp.

00:11:47.750 --> 00:11:49.750
Senkawa...

00:11:49.750 --> 00:11:52.250
The people lost their homes, and
were cut off from the community,

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:56.060
but still lived as best they could...

00:11:56.060 --> 00:11:58.860
Are the monsters killing each other?

00:11:58.860 --> 00:12:00.160
Valic...

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:03.330
Maybe we should run while the
lxiorans have their death match.

00:12:03.330 --> 00:12:06.570
That's the kind of idea a vulgar Altan would have.

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:09.740
Did you kill Gatol?

00:12:09.740 --> 00:12:12.340
Sheesh, Ulgarians are so nasty.

00:12:12.340 --> 00:12:14.240
Well, I'm running away.

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:19.380
Then get lost already. I won't
survive only to live in shame.

00:12:19.380 --> 00:12:21.450
Huh?

00:12:21.450 --> 00:12:25.290
You bitch! You started up
the time bomb, didn't you?!

00:12:25.290 --> 00:12:29.190
That's why I'm telling you to scram fast.

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:31.690
These are children that
we met in the refugee camp.

00:12:31.690 --> 00:12:35.360
We also met a lot of other people.

00:12:35.360 --> 00:12:41.570
None of them were possessed by grief or hatred.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:45.400
What was there... was love.

00:12:52.650 --> 00:12:54.050
What are you trying to do, Birdy?!

00:12:54.050 --> 00:12:56.050
I'm going to take Nataru to the Lailalo.

00:12:56.050 --> 00:12:57.040
But...

00:13:00.460 --> 00:13:04.160
It's kind of embarrassing to talk about "love,"

00:13:04.160 --> 00:13:08.990
but I can't think of any other way to express it.

00:13:12.770 --> 00:13:15.800
Nataru, come with me to the Lailalo!

00:13:15.800 --> 00:13:17.270
Fight me, Birdy!

00:13:17.270 --> 00:13:20.080
I don't want to!

00:13:20.080 --> 00:13:24.680
You have to kill me with your lxioran powers.

00:13:24.680 --> 00:13:27.520
Lailalo, the gate!

00:13:27.520 --> 00:13:30.920
If I give you a tune-up in the Lailalo,
you can go back to how you were!

00:13:30.920 --> 00:13:35.590
A "tune-up"? That itself is
proof I'm a damned lxioran!

00:13:35.590 --> 00:13:36.580
Nataru?!

00:13:39.260 --> 00:13:41.090
Fight, Birdy!

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:46.920
Nataru!

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:53.040
They've cast off traits they'd
acquired on the journey to adulthood,

00:13:53.040 --> 00:13:56.480
and returned to the purity and honesty of youth...

00:14:01.280 --> 00:14:06.320
I think we have to make sure
we don't forget this feeling.

00:14:06.320 --> 00:14:10.860
Sheesh, that's so pitiful, fighting until you die...

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:14.300
Thank God <i>I wasn't born an lxioran.</i>

00:14:15.660 --> 00:14:20.400
Valic! Valic! Go, hurry!

00:14:20.400 --> 00:14:21.840
It's terrorists!

00:14:28.840 --> 00:14:32.840
No... I don't want to die!

00:14:34.080 --> 00:14:39.020
Sheesh... Dying gets you nothing.

00:14:39.020 --> 00:14:41.720
I'll take my dad's place.

00:14:41.720 --> 00:14:43.760
This is a suicide bombing, you know!

00:14:43.760 --> 00:14:45.590
That's fine. I'll do it.

00:14:47.760 --> 00:14:50.570
He's been like this since he was a kid...

00:14:50.570 --> 00:14:52.190
Fight, Birdy!

00:14:53.670 --> 00:14:56.260
Show me the power of an lxioran!

00:14:58.410 --> 00:14:59.400
Nataru!

00:15:01.940 --> 00:15:02.930
Birdy!

00:15:12.550 --> 00:15:15.120
Birdy! Birdy, wake up!

00:15:15.120 --> 00:15:16.110
Birdy!

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:19.380
Ow!

00:15:26.270 --> 00:15:28.100
I have to help...

00:15:29.810 --> 00:15:31.800
Please stop this, Nataru.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:38.550
I'm inside Birdy right now.

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:44.490
So I know everything about you, too.
Everything Birdy saw.

00:15:44.490 --> 00:15:47.490
Why are you?

00:15:47.490 --> 00:15:51.790
Birdy is loaning me her body to keep me alive.

00:15:51.790 --> 00:15:54.230
So I'll protect Birdy!

00:15:55.900 --> 00:16:00.500
She's an lxioran, but she wasn't born just to fight.

00:16:00.500 --> 00:16:04.840
She can keep saving people's lives, too!

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:08.780
I think it's <i>because</i> she's
Birdy that she can do that.

00:16:08.780 --> 00:16:12.310
So Nataru...

00:16:12.310 --> 00:16:13.300
Tsutomu.

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:17.470
Birdy...

00:16:19.990 --> 00:16:21.360
I...

00:16:21.360 --> 00:16:22.350
Nataru...

00:16:25.490 --> 00:16:26.480
Birdy...

00:16:58.960 --> 00:16:59.950
Birdy.

00:17:06.170 --> 00:17:09.140
Thank you, Birdy.

00:17:09.140 --> 00:17:12.640
Now I know there's something I can do, too.

00:17:12.640 --> 00:17:14.640
Why?

00:17:14.640 --> 00:17:17.480
There's something I want to tell you.

00:17:17.480 --> 00:17:19.310
Will you listen?

00:17:39.100 --> 00:17:43.040
I'll come to see you, Birdy.

00:17:43.040 --> 00:17:44.030
Nataru?

00:17:54.180 --> 00:17:55.170
Nataru...

00:18:08.100 --> 00:18:11.930
I guess I'm a big softy, huh?

00:18:29.320 --> 00:18:31.750
Success! That was a huge success!

00:18:31.750 --> 00:18:34.060
The whole audience was really moved.

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:36.320
Yeah, it makes our hard work worth it.

00:18:36.320 --> 00:18:36.660
"Journalism Club"
Yeah, it makes our hard work worth it.

00:18:36.660 --> 00:18:39.130
I was touched!
"Journalism Club"

00:18:39.130 --> 00:18:39.320
That was so good, Hayamiya!
"Journalism Club"

00:18:39.320 --> 00:18:41.300
That was so good, Hayamiya!

00:18:41.300 --> 00:18:42.560
It moves a guy to tears!

00:18:42.560 --> 00:18:44.470
It's thanks to all of you.

00:18:44.470 --> 00:18:47.140
Senkawa never came, huh?

00:18:47.140 --> 00:18:52.240
Don't worry about it, Hayamiya. I'm sure...

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:54.830
...I'll be able to see him again.

00:18:58.980 --> 00:18:59.970
Where?

00:19:06.920 --> 00:19:07.910
Where?

00:19:25.440 --> 00:19:27.430
This place is...

00:19:31.210 --> 00:19:32.200
Violin...

00:19:34.780 --> 00:19:35.770
Birdy...

00:19:42.460 --> 00:19:43.450
Shit!

00:20:10.850 --> 00:20:12.720
Stop.

00:20:12.720 --> 00:20:16.690
Death isn't your role right now.

00:20:16.690 --> 00:20:17.990
Protect her.

00:20:17.990 --> 00:20:19.560
Birdy!

00:20:19.560 --> 00:20:22.100
Protect her future.

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:26.090
Get out of here, fast. Protect that girl.

00:20:30.270 --> 00:20:33.710
The arrest of Moss Kiri is deeply meaningful.

00:20:33.710 --> 00:20:36.240
I'm sure the repercussions of
her testimony about the incident

00:20:36.240 --> 00:20:38.280
will affect the very nerve
center of our government.

00:20:38.280 --> 00:20:43.590
That was the reason your request
for reinforcements was smothered.

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:47.760
Captain Megius, what
about the data I requested?

00:20:47.760 --> 00:20:51.890
About secret research on
lxiorans regarding jump abilities?

00:20:51.890 --> 00:20:54.430
It seems that never happened.

00:20:54.430 --> 00:20:57.900
That can't be true! Most of the experiments failed,

00:20:57.900 --> 00:21:00.770
but the rare successes were born with jump abilities

00:21:00.770 --> 00:21:02.970
in exchange for low biodefense...

00:21:02.970 --> 00:21:06.880
It never happened, Birdy.

00:21:06.880 --> 00:21:10.980
This investigation is over.

00:21:10.980 --> 00:21:14.210
They had the power to leap through time.

00:21:28.830 --> 00:21:29.820
Shoko.

00:21:34.470 --> 00:21:36.570
So, what did you want with me?

00:21:36.570 --> 00:21:38.770
You better not have come
to say you're marrying Nataru

00:21:38.770 --> 00:21:40.940
and rub my face in it.

00:21:40.940 --> 00:21:43.010
It's not like that!

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:46.680
I just wanted to see you able to walk.

00:21:46.680 --> 00:21:49.280
Hey, is Nataru doing okay?

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:52.820
Yeah. That's what he said in his letter.

00:21:52.820 --> 00:21:56.020
Man, I wanted to walk down this path with him...

00:21:56.020 --> 00:21:58.690
Why did he go abroad all of a sudden?

00:21:58.690 --> 00:22:00.260
That reminds me.

00:22:00.260 --> 00:22:02.830
A present for you from Nataru.

00:22:02.830 --> 00:22:05.130
He could've just sent it directly to me!

00:22:05.130 --> 00:22:08.840
What's with the buffer? That makes
me not happy about it, somehow.

00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:10.510
What is this?

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:12.500
You go like this.

00:22:14.340 --> 00:22:16.780
Wow! Let me see that!

00:22:18.110 --> 00:22:24.890
Whoa, what is this thing? It's so awesome! Cool!

00:22:24.890 --> 00:22:27.520
A Christmas present from me.

00:22:27.520 --> 00:22:32.150
If you run across Nataru, tell
him I want to see him again.

00:22:54.050 --> 00:22:59.040
<i>I'll be waiting for you, Nataru.</i>

00:23:14.000 --> 00:23:14.600
"News Flash"

00:23:14.600 --> 00:23:16.710
<i>This is Shion Arita, yessiree!</i>

00:23:16.710 --> 00:23:17.770
Unauthorized reproduction is prohibited."

00:23:17.770 --> 00:23:19.870
<i>It's been a long time since we talked!</i>

00:23:19.870 --> 00:23:25.410
<i>This time Ms. Irma has promised</i>
<i>I'll do concerts, yessiree...</i>

00:23:25.410 --> 00:23:27.780
<i>In Kobe, no less!</i>

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:33.090
<i>And would you believe it...Tsutomu's</i>
<i>beloved Nakasugi is there, yessiree!</i>

00:23:33.090 --> 00:23:35.590
<i>But someone is targeting her...</i>

00:23:35.590 --> 00:23:40.790
<i>"Oh, no! Birdy, help me!"</i>
